The Day 238 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 9 KB). The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the file and the || true let the step pass anyway. The file is on disk for the planner, but it isn't in git unless someone adds it with -f.

• Build and runs: the harness had already verified this commit. I ran the binary once with a prompt (it answered PONG, exit 0) and ran yoyo doctor (12/12 checks passed). The last 4 evolve runs and the last 5 CI runs all passed, with no reverts in the 14-day window.
• Probes:
  • Issue #1072 is mostly fixed. In a fresh git init folder, doctor now shows branch: master instead of detached.
  • Issue #1075 is still live. doctor still tells shell users to run /init and /remember, which only exist inside the chat window.
• Backlog: there are 24 open agent-self issues. The ones with clear scope that don't need the owner to decide anything first are #1077 (/bg kill says the job is killed but the shell keeps running), #1075, #1062, #1057 and #1068.
• Competitor scan: I read Claude Code's changelog up to 2.1.310 and Codex 0.164, and saved the useful parts to yopedia. Four items match open work here:
  • Claude Code now loads only the start of an oversized CLAUDE.md. Our #1070 slice only warns, and still sends the whole file every turn.
  • Claude Code fixed --worktree deleting a worktree at exit and losing commits. That's the same kind of bug as our #1057.
  • Claude Code fixed hook processes left running after a stop. That's the same kind of bug as our #1077.
  • Claude Code fixed a deny rule that didn't block a bash redirect to the denied path inside a subshell. I didn't probe whether yoyo has the same hole.
• Notes for the planner:
  • #1012 (wrong prices in /cost) has nothing left that you can pick from the model menu. All 48 remaining rows are only reached by typing a model name. Price fixes took the second task in 4 of the last 6 sessions, so it's worth deciding in writing whether this still beats the items above.
  • #1078 is about a protected file, so it stays a question for the owner, not a task.
  • For #1064 (API keys leaking to child processes), stopping MCP servers from inheriting the key is the clear next step. Read @yuanhao's latest comment before changing the default for the model's own shell.
